So the RNG rolled up Burper the Neutral Human Cavewoman, and despite no
real good equipment finds in the early game, save a Gauntlets of Power
some dwarf dropped. I made it through the Mines without a problem,
tamed a few horses and dogs and ripped off a large ring shop on DLVL 3
for almost all their inventory. An early pickax drop by a dwarf let me
buy protection, and I got 4 pts on the first try. Despite the GoP,
encumbrance was already a problem by Sokoban, and no bag of holding.I
finally accumlated several bags and figured out which was the holding.

No shortage of altars either. An early sacrifice gave Giantslayer.. big
whoop. I used the +1 Club for most of the game. Cleaned out Fort
Ludicrous, made it down to Medusas and still no levitation. Now this
was fun, because I usually feel I *need* levitation, but this time, I
just dug down and hoped to find boots in Perseus' statue.

The pit dropped me 2 levels and by the time I'd mazed my way up to
Medusa I'd forgotten to blind myself!! My heart stopped for a second,
but then.. Medusa's gaze reflects from your medallion. Medusa is
killed! Whew. Whoops, no levboots here. I had the ingenious idea of
reading my scrolls of Earth from Sokoban to fill a path, but didn't get
enough boulders. Went down and did the castle, Finally found a wand of
Cold and made a path, ready to go up and do the Quest.

Although I zapped The Chromatic Dragon with a wand of death a couple
times, he woke up and hurt me badly and I quickly wished up a set of
armor, taking me down to -24 from -11 and getting me speed boots and
GDSM. Using only my +1 Club I managed to kill the Chromatic Dragon
after a very long, protracted fight. I dunno if it was because I was
drunk, bored, or just that I anticipated a boring time mapping out
Gehennom manually, but when I ate his corpse (I was satiated, but just
barely), and got the "Stop eating?" message, I just decided to take the
chance.. You die. If only I'd had a tinning kit!

What's silly is, the only intrinsic I really needed was shock
resistance. I guess this is more like a suicide than anything, but I
must admit that I'm not unpleased with the result - my #2 high score
says "Burper, choked on the Chromatic Dragon's corpse." Hey, at least
that proves I killed the MF!



